  "notes": "First bench sitting after Waves 0-2 of the RadiANT refactor (the ANTW_*/antr_* seam). The image under test is the refactored sdk_ant backend, not the pre-refactor dist/ant_dongle.uf2: CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_RADIO_SDK_ANT=y, CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_TRANSPORT_USB_LEGACY=y, CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_ENCRYPTION=n. FLASH 117356 B / RAM 42888 B.\n\nThere is no B leg in this sitting. ant_core does not exist yet, so both radio runs are A. They are recorded as a pair on purpose: two consecutive 300 s runs on an unmoved rig both read loss (exact) 0.26 %, which is the bottom of the 0.26-0.60 % characterised floor and fixes the run-to-run spread for this sitting at essentially zero. That is what a future A/B/A has to be read against.\n\nUnexplained loss is 0 in both runs: 3 missing packets, 3 EVENT_RX_FAIL, in each. Note the event name - ant_verify.py now emits EVENT_-prefixed names from the generated table, and loss_accounting() accepts both spellings.\n\ngit_describe is -dirty because the working tree carries the artifacts this sitting produced (this file, the two .antcap captures and the .antser transcript). No source file was modified for the measurement.\n\nDeliberately absent, not zero-filled: `sensitivity` (needs an inline attenuator or a human to move the boards through a distance sweep - neither was available unattended, and re-running the transmit-power sweep instead is explicitly closed); `scale` (libant.a allocates 8 channels, so there is nothing to measure at 32); `ack_data` (ant_session.py's acknowledged-data probe was accepted and queued by the stack but the channel stopped tracking before it went out, so no success rate can be claimed - measuring one needs a held master/slave pair, which sim/ does not provide)."
